cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the article it accompanies (preferred-citation below)."
type: software
title: "Adaptive basis texture tomography of simulated data"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Carøe"
    given-names: "Martin Sæbye"
    affiliation: "Technical University of Denmark"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3739-7562"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/msaca-okse/adaptive_basis_simulation"
abstract: >-
  Notebooks that reconstruct two simulated scanning 3DXRD datasets of an aluminium polycrystal (1 and
  10 degree intra-granular mosaicity) by texture tomography with an adaptive orientation basis built
  from point-by-point indexing, and compare them with a uniform orientation grid and the ground truth.
keywords:
  - texture tomography
  - s3DXRD
  - scanning 3DXRD
  - adaptive basis
  - simulated data
